      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Occupying one of Clontarf's most prestigious residential addresses, No. 187 Mount Prospect Avenue is an exceptional detached family home standing proudly on a generous wraparound corner site with an enclosed private south-facing rear garden, two separate vehicular entrances and extensive frontage. Set well back from the road behind mature planting, the property enjoys an abundance of privacy, outstanding outdoor space and exceptional potential in one of Dublin's most sought-after coastal suburbs.\r\n\r\nExtending to approximately 199.4 sq. m. (2,146 sq. ft.), the accommodation has evolved over the years to create a wonderfully versatile home suited to a variety of lifestyles. Whether you are seeking a substantial family residence, accommodation for multi-generational living, independent guest quarters or a property with scope to remodel and extend, No. 187 offers an exceptional opportunity.\r\n\r\nA welcoming entrance porch leads to a spacious reception hall, setting the tone for the generous accommodation beyond. The elegant living room is beautifully proportioned, filled with natural light and provides an ideal space for both everyday family living and entertaining. The kitchen and breakfast room forms the heart of the home, offering ample space for dining and direct access to the enclosed private south-facing rear garden, where mature planting creates a wonderfully sheltered and secluded outdoor setting.\r\n\r\nThe current layout comprises five well-proportioned bedrooms, including a principal suite with dressing room and en-suite bathroom. A separate wing has been arranged as self-contained accommodation with its own entrance, bedrooms, bathroom and utility facilities, making it ideal for extended family, independent living, guest accommodation or a home-based business. The large attic room provides valuable additional space and lends itself equally well to a home office, studio, playroom or hobby room.\r\n\r\nThe generous wraparound site is undoubtedly one of the property's defining features. With two independent driveways, extensive frontage and gardens surrounding the house, the property offers enormous flexibility for those wishing to further extend, reconfigure the existing accommodation or explore future redevelopment potential, subject to the necessary planning permission.\r\n\r\nMount Prospect Avenue is widely regarded as one of Clontarf's finest residential locations. The entrance to the historic Rose Garden in St. Anne's Park is just a few steps away, while the renowned Pitch 35 is directly opposite. Residents enjoy immediate access to acres of parkland, woodland walks, children's playgrounds, sporting facilities and the Clontarf promenade. The area is exceptionally well served by an excellent choice of primary and secondary schools, together with golf, rugby, tennis, GAA, cricket, sailing and numerous other recreational amenities. Clontarf Road and Killester DART Stations, regular Dublin Bus services and convenient access to the city centre, East Point Business Park, the IFSC, Dublin Airport, the M1 and M50 complete this outstanding location.\r\n\r\nHomes of this calibre, occupying such substantial sites in this location, rarely come to the market. Combining generous accommodation, exceptional gardens, remarkable flexibility and significant potential to further enhance or reconfigure, No. 187 represents a rare opportunity to acquire a landmark family home in one of Clontarf's most established and sought-after locations."
      },
